 ________________________________\nFrom: David Lindberg <dlindberg@outlyr.c
 om>\nSent: Monday\, August 31\, 2026 3:14 PM\nTo: Alec Kennedy <alec_kenne
 dy@b-f.com>\; Sandy Diamond <SDiamond@outlyr.com>\nSubject: Re: Chubb Clas
 sic follow up\n\nHi Alec-\n\nGreat to hear from you and no worries at all!
 \n\nYes\, we are available on Thursday morning. Would 9am work or somewher
 e around then? If so\, I can pass along a calendar invite for then.\n\nTha
 nk you!\n\nAll the best\,\nDavid\n\n\n\n\n[Icon  Description automatically
  generated]\n\nDavid Lindberg | Sales Director\n\na: 6722 Lone Oak Blvd\, 
 Naples\, FL 34109\ne: dlindberg@outlyr.com<mailto:dlindberg@outlyr.com> | 
 w: www.chubbclassic.com<http:// www.chubbclassic.com>\np: (315) 663-6924\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n________________________________\nFrom: Alec Kennedy <alec_ke
 nnedy@b-f.com>\nSent: Monday\, August 31\, 2026 11:50 AM\nTo: David Lindbe
 rg <dlindberg@outlyr.com>\; Sandy Diamond <SDiamond@outlyr.com>\nSubject: 
 Re: Chubb Classic follow up\n\nMy apologies\, August was crazy. Are you al
 l available this Thursday?\n\n________________________________\nFrom: Davi
 d Lindberg <dlindberg@outlyr.com>\nSent: Monday\, 31 August 2026 11:36:10\
 nTo: Sandy Diamond <SDiamond@outlyr.com>\; Alec Kennedy <alec_kennedy@b-f.
 com>\nSubject: Re: Chubb Classic follow up\n\nHi Alec-\n\nWe trust all is 
 going well and how is your son doing??? Have you been able to sleep throug
 h the night now?\n\nSandy and I wanted to send along a quick note to see i
 f you have some time to regroup with us over the next couple of weeks by c
 hance? If so\, could you kindly share a few dates and times that would wor
 k best?\n\nThank you so much and looking forward to hearing back from you 
 shortly!\n\nAll the best\,\nDavid\n\n\n\n[Icon  Description automatically 
 generated]\n\nDavid Lindberg | Sales Director\n\na: 6722 Lone Oak Blvd\, N
 aples\, FL 34109\ne: dlindberg@outlyr.com<mailto:dlindberg@outlyr.com> | w
 : www.chubbclassic.com<http:// www.chubbclassic.com>\np: (315) 663-6924\n
 \n\n\n\n\n\n________________________________\nFrom: Sandy Diamond <SDiamon
 d@outlyr.com>\nSent: Tuesday\, August 4\, 2026 10:30 AM\nTo: alec_kennedy@
 b-f.com <alec_kennedy@b-f.com>\nCc: David Lindberg <dlindberg@outlyr.com>\
 nSubject: FW: Chubb Classic follow up\n\n\nAlec\,\n\n\n\nHow are you and t
 he family?  How is “my godson” Lorenzo?????\n\n\n\nFirst\, thank you s
 o much again for taking care of Grayson (the head of agronomy/superintende
 nt) at Tiburon…he was so appreciative.  I think Eddy had a great day pla
 ying too…glad everything worked out perfectly.\n\n\n\nI wanted to circle
  back per our last correspondences to see if we can get our Chubb Classic 
 tournament partnership in place.  We have LOVED partnering with you and Jo
 hnny and look forward to many more successful tournaments together!  I bel
 ieve you mentioned August was a good time to reconnect…we will follow yo
 ur lead on next steps.\n\n\n\nThank you so much again for being such an in
 tegral part of the Chubb Classic…we appreciate you and Johnny very much!
 \n\n\n\nWarm regards\,\n\n\n\n\n\n[Icon  Description automatically generat
 ed]\n\nSandy Diamond |Senior Vice President\, Executive Director\n\na: 672
 2 Lone Oak Blvd\, Naples\, FL 34109\ne: [sdiamond@outlyr.com ]sdiamond@out
 lyr.com | w: www.chubbclassic.com<http:// www.chubbclassic.com>\nc: (201)
  206-2073\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Sandy Diamond\nSent: Friday\, June 5\, 2026 10:
 38 AM\nTo: alec_kennedy@b-f.com\; johnny_williams@b-f.com\nCc: David Lindb
 erg <dlindberg@outlyr.com>\nSubject: Chubb Classic follow up\n\n\n\nAlec a
 nd Johnny\,\n\n\n\nJust a quick note to thank you both for reconnecting wi
 th David and me yesterday regarding our ’27 Chubb Classic partnership.\n
 \n\n\nWe were delighted to hear that the program continues to prove most w
 orthwhile and delivers a strong ROI.  We are also thrilled with our partne
 rship\, and I know both Par Catering and Tiburon Golf Club (a Troon proper
 ty) really like working with Brown-Forman as well.\n\n\n\nPer our discussi
 on\, we will follow up next month to reconnect and barring anything unfore
 seen with your budgets\, look forward to having you back in the fold once 
 again.  As I mentioned\, this will be the 40th consecutive playing of our 
 event (in the same market)\, we are the longest running PGA TOUR Champions
  tournament to have that very cool distinction.  Maybe we create a 40th An
 niversary “celebration cocktail”…we can discuss further when we get 
 a bit closer to the tournament.\n\n\n\nThank you both SO much again for al
 l that you do to support us…Alec\, have a great weekend with the family 
 and Johnny\, have an awesome time at our old stomping grounds in Central N
 Y…enjoy the Dark Horse and the other local bars too!\n\n\n\nWarm regards
 \,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n[Icon  Description automatically generated]\n\nSandy Dia
 mond |Senior Vice President\, Executive Director\n\na: 6722 Lone Oak Blvd\
 , Naples\, FL 34109\ne: [sdiamond@outlyr.com ]sdiamond@outlyr.com | w: www
 .chubbclassic.com<http:// www.chubbclassic.com>\nc: (201) 206-2073\n\n\n\
 n\n\n_____________________________________________________________________
